Subject: [PATCH 05040/11362] [outer-loop] runbook: CUDA 12.8 binary now Docker
 cross-built + pre-staged (no Kaggle build step)

Cross-built the Kaggle-compatible llama-server via nvidia/cuda:12.8.1-devel on the
dev box (nvcc emits SASS for the listed archs regardless of host GPU; toolkit stub
libcuda.so at link time, real driver from Kaggle at runtime). Archs 60/75/86/89.
Smoke-validated on the 3090 via the exact main.py copy-to-/kaggle/working path:
binary copied out of its lib dir, libs resolved via LD_LIBRARY_PATH=server.parent,
loads CUDA0, generates. Staged 12-SONAME .so closure as real files (no symlinks,
robust to Kaggle dataset upload). Submission now fully self-contained.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
